us (HIV) infection patterns and risk behaviours in different population groups and provinces in Viet Nam</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>2007</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17242756</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khuat</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HIV/AIDS policy in Viet Nam: A Civil Society Perspective</article-title><year>2007</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.soros.org/initiatives/health/focus/phw/articles_publications/publications/vietnam_20071129/vietnam_20071129.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hammett</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Duc</surname><given-names>TT</given-names></name><name><surname>Stephens</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Sullivan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ngu</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Des Jarlais</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>'Social evils' and harm reduction: the evolving policy environment for human immunodeficiency virus prevention among injection drug users in China and Vietnam</article-title><source>Addiction</source><year>2008</year><volume>103</volume><fpage>137</fpage><lpage>145</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18028519</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1360-0443.2007.02053.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gammeltoft</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Seeking trust and transcendence: sexual risk-taking among Vietnamese youth</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>483</fpage><lpage>496</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12144154</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0277-9536(01)00182-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thuy</surname><given-names>NT</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindan</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Phong</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Van</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Nhung</surname><given-names>VT</given-names></name><name><surname>Barclay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Khiem</surname><given-names>HB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predictors of visits to commercial sex workers by male attendees at sexually transmitted disease clinics in southern Vietnam</article-title><source>Aids</source><year>1999</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>719</fpage><lpage>725</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10397567</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00002030-199904160-00013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ball</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HIV, injecting drug use and harm reduction: a public health response</article-title><source>Addiction</source><year>2007</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>684</fpage><lpage>690</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17506148</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1360-0443.2007.01761.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wodak</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>McLeod</surname><given-names>L</g